- core/stats/response_surface.py: response_surface — linear,
  interaction, quadratic or cubic surface in two variates (raw or centred),
  sequential ANOVA with Remainder (lack of fit) against pure error from
  replicates or a supplied ResMS/df when rows are treatment means
  (Tables 17.8, 17.10), marginality-respecting backward selection
  (Example 17.3B), parameters with SE (Tables 17.9, 17.11), share of
  treatment variation explained, expansion to uncentred coefficients,
  fitted surface on a 21 × 21 grid.
- core/stats/nonlinear.py: nonlinear_regression — exponential, inverse
  linear, logistic, Gompertz and power curves by least squares (grid
  start over the nonlinear parameters, then Levenberg–Marquardt),
  approximate SEs s²(JᵀJ)⁻¹, delta-method prediction bands, asymptotes,
  warning for a degenerate S-curve (Example 17.1C); curve_comparison —
  ResMS, adjusted R², AIC, SBC for transformations, polynomials and
  nonlinear curves (Table 17.12).
- Tests against Tables 17.8–17.12, Examples 17.1C, 17.3A, 17.3B
  (Table 17.7 data added); S-curve SEs checked vs scipy curve_fit.
- Catalog, i18n, bridge, messages.

